@@ -32,6 +32,10 @@ Fizzy uses **URL path-based multi-tenancy**:
 
 Passwordless magic link authentication. A global `Identity` (email-based) can have `Users` in multiple Accounts, so an email is not a single account membership. Users have roles: owner, admin, member, system. Board-level access control via `Access` records.
 
+### Account Cancellation & Incineration
+
+Cancelling an account (`Account#cancel`) records an `Account::Cancellation` and makes the account inactive right away, but keeps its data so it can be reactivated. Once `Account::Incineratable::INCINERATION_GRACE_PERIOD` (30 days) has passed, the recurring `Account::IncinerateDueJob` incinerates the account, permanently deleting everything in it: database rows, search index entries, storage ledger entries, and uploaded files.
+
 ### Entropy System
 
 Cards automatically "postpone" (move to "not now") after inactivity:
